course: dictionary
lesson: 1599
title: Cheddar: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Cheddar is first a cheese: a hard, yellow or orange-yellow cheese from the village of Cheddar in Somerset, England. «Many food words are traps for English ears: syrnYky are made with soft cottage cheese, not cheddar.» Here cheddar is the hard cheese, set against the soft cheese in syrnYky.
explain: The word can also be a place name. Cheddar is a village in England, famous for Cheddar Gorge and its caves. A capital C in the middle of a sentence is a clue that you are reading about a place. Ask yourself: is this about food, a village, or money?
explain: In American slang, cheddar means money, like «dough». If someone says, «He's got a lot of cheddar», he has a lot of money, not a lot of cheese. Words like shop, pay or wallet are clues. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: Cheddar is a hard cheese, yellow or orange-yellow, and it can taste mild or strong.
fact: Cheddar cheese was first made in the village of Cheddar in Somerset, England.
fact: Cheddar is the most popular cheese in the UK, Ireland, Australia, Canada and New Zealand.
fact: In US slang, «cheddar» means money, like «dough».
fact: Cheddar Gorge is a limestone gorge with caves, where cheese was once stored.
exercise: «Put a slice of cheddar on your sandwich.» What is cheddar here? | Money | *A hard, yellow cheese | A kind of bread | A village in England
exercise: «He's got a lot of cheddar», says Sam's cousin from the US. What does cheddar mean here? | A pile of cheese | A hard, yellow cheese | *Money | A village in Somerset
exercise: «Cheddar Gorge is famous for its caves.» What is Cheddar in this sentence? | Money | A hard, yellow cheese | *A place in England with a famous gorge | A kind of drink
test: «Many food words are traps for English ears: syrnYky are made with soft cottage cheese, not cheddar.» Which statement about cheddar is true? | It is a drink, like kompOt | It is a soft cheese, like cottage cheese | It is a kind of bread | *It is a hard cheese
test: A shop sign says «Cheddar, 2 for 1». Which meaning fits best? | Money | *A hard, yellow cheese | A village in England | A caves tour
exam: Which of these is NOT a meaning of cheddar? | A village in England | Money, in US slang | *A kind of drink, like kompOt | A hard, yellow cheese
